/-!
# Odd Hall geometry for the chosen natural shadow

The literal relative Hall subgroup has order dividing q-1, its source D0
lies in L and normalizes T intersect L, and its natural rank-one quotient
contains a nonidentity split diagonal after a constructed basis change.
The source assembly chooses a permitted Cartan containing D0 and applies
the diagonal to the existing natural fixed-space argument.

The earlier-source residual clauses, SL3/Sp4 alternative and natural marking
remain explicit, as required by their separate source producers. The
L-module dichotomy and full 11.3.7 assembly remain with the Cartan owner.
Source: Aschbacher--Smith, 11.0.4 and 11.3.7(2,3,5), printed pp.760,773.
-/
